{"c":[{"id":"f9666f0bda0d6429","sum":"Host: repeating KeyframeAnimator redraws off screen (10.9% CPU; use Timer blinks); debug JSON omits nil, test == null. XCTestCase.record(_:) shadows a free record(...): name it taskRecord. Perch checks run headless: real Helper, fake-app.ts reader, --perch hidden, pid 5150.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"40c277ae98ccebf5","sum":"A repeating SwiftUI KeyframeAnimator redraws every frame even off screen (perch blink+breath cost 10.9% of a core; one-shot Timer blinks ~1%). The host's debug-socket JSON omits nil optionals, so scripts test == null, not === null.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T213409Z-2c06a8e735f40a5c","text":"A repeating SwiftUI KeyframeAnimator redraws every frame, even through long holds and in a panel never ordered on screen: the perch's 5 s blink plus breath cost the host 10.9% of a core; one-shot blinks on a Timer cost about 1%.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T213409Z-cab3b62b740f0600","text":"The host's debug-socket JSON omits nil optionals (Swift JSONEncoder), so scripts must test == null / undefined, not === null.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b1c45b8f5a3c01de","sum":"Tests: in XCTestCase subclasses a free function record(...) is shadowed by XCTestCase.record(_:), so name builders taskRecord. Perch/taskControl checks run with nothing on screen: real Helper with helper/test/fake-app.ts as readerLink, host --perch hidden --allow-pids 5150.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T213409Z-d226423d62147f07","text":"In XCTestCase subclasses a free function named record(...) is shadowed by XCTestCase.record(_:); name test builders taskRecord or similar.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T213410Z-c55d0036facdd019","text":"Perch and taskControl checks can run with nothing on screen: real Helper in process with helper/test/fake-app.ts as readerLink, host with --perch hidden and --allow-pids 5150 (no such process).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"aa279d8cb1624e15","sum":"apps/caret: SurfaceMachine/FillMachine decide, coordinators only read and draw; test with SurfaceRig/FillRig and a ManualClock. ImageRenderer draws AppKit controls as placeholders: render SwiftUI-drawn ones. Host tests: own --settings, --status-item off.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97ae8d03f0e99759","sum":"x","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T020832Z-18f641c9e903d593","text":"apps/caret: surface decisions (hold, retry, withdraw, work line, toast undo, Esc/Cmd-Z) live in CaretHostCore SurfaceMachine; SurfaceCoordinator only reads AppKit and draws. Test a surface change with SurfaceRig steps and a ManualClock, not on screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T022431Z-7481bd50921d0954","text":"apps/caret: fill decisions (proposal hold, withdraw, toast lifetime, its Cmd-Z grant) live in CaretHostCore FillMachine; FillCoordinator only reads AX and draws. Test with FillRig; the shared toast slot with SharedToastSlotTests.TwoOwners (one arbiter).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"fea98e93de0597e3","sum":"ImageRenderer draws AppKit controls (Button, Toggle, ProgressView) as placeholders: off-screen renders need SwiftUI-drawn controls, as OnboardingView does. Host test runs: pass --settings <own file> and --status-item off; --onboarding defaults off.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T024925Z-053830fa0ce54d2d","text":"SwiftUI ImageRenderer draws AppKit-backed controls (stock Button, Toggle, ProgressView) as placeholders; off-screen renders of a window need every control drawn in SwiftUI with custom styles, as Onboarding/OnboardingView does.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T024925Z-d69b7ed0397e33f9","text":"Caret host test runs: pass --settings <own file> and --status-item off; --onboarding defaults to off so a launch never puts a window up (auto opens it until finished once).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
